2. ALEXA ALEV III spectral sensitivity estimate (data/alexa/)
   Our own estimate (Apache-2.0), fitted to the ARRI matrices above (AMPAS
   licence, see 1) with a spectral prior built from rawtoaces-data (see 3).
   It is an estimate, not a measurement.

3. rawtoaces-data (data/cameras/sony/)
   Sony camera spectral sensitivity measurements by Weta Digital and the
   190-patch training reflectance set, from
   https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/rawtoaces-data,
   Apache License 2.0 (data/cameras/sony/LICENSE-rawtoaces-data).

4. ACES 2.0 output transform
   Rust port of the CTL reference in https://github.com/aces-aswf/aces-core
   (commit 069b0bc) with the output presets of
   https://github.com/aces-aswf/aces-output (commit 6d8f907).
   Apache License 2.0. Copyright Contributors to the ACES Project.

5. Figtree typeface
   Copyright 2022 The Figtree Project Authors
   (https://github.com/erikdkennedy/figtree). SIL Open Font License 1.1; the
   licence text is in THIRD-PARTY.md inside the app (design/fonts/OFL.txt in
   the repository).

6. Training data for shipped model weights
   The weights that ship (data/models/illum, the illuminant estimators) are
   fitted on synthetic scenes only: reflectances from rawtoaces-data (see 3),
   illuminant spectra from the CIE (CC BY-SA 4.0) and spectra we generate,
   seen through the published camera curves. No shipped weights are trained
   on photographs.
   See data/models/*/MODEL_CARD.md for per-model provenance. Datasets such as
   PixelShift200 and Cube++ (both CC BY 4.0) are credited here when weights
   trained on them ship.

